  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SANTIAGUILLO LAGOON I</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Santiaguillo Lagoon, the largest wetland in the state of Durango, is historically important to Northern Pintails, Blue-winged Teals, Snow Goose, and White-fronted Goose. It is also important for the Mexican Duck, a threatened, resident species. This wetland is an Important Bird Area, is one of the 28 Mexican priority wetlands for wintering waterfowl, and is a RAMSAR site. This project will protect 18,327.4 acres in Santiaguillo Lagoon and restore the seasonal wetlands on 9,880 of those acres. It will also enhance 177.84 acres of wetlands on communal lands.</narrative>
  </description>
